          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "7.4 Marking Fraction Lengths on the Number Line"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.162,
            0.834,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": "We have marked lengths equal to 1, 2, 3, … units on the number line. Now, let us try to mark lengths equal to fractions on the number line."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.208,
            0.833,
            0.254
          ],
          "content": "What is the length of the blue line? Write the fraction that gives the length of the blue line in the box."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.264,
            0.807,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.338,
            0.834,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": "The distance between 0 and 1 is one unit long. It is divided into two equal parts. So, the length of each part is $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ unit. So, this blue line is $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ unit long."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.423,
            0.833,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": "Now, can you find the lengths of the various blue lines shown below? Fill in the boxes as well."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.468,
            0.834,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": "1. Here, the fractional unit is dividing a length of 1 unit into three equal parts. Write the fraction that gives the length of the blue line in the box or in your notebook."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
